- I like it.

00:07:38.843 --> 00:07:39.960
- Well, it was all words
that applied to me, I think.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.067
- Yeah.
- So.

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:42.030
- Used them.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:46.020
- Used them, and I was very
worried when we first did it,

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.943
when I've recorded the first
tracks, I got them ready,

00:07:48.943 --> 00:07:51.750
and then he came in and he started dancing

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.370
and then I knew everything,

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.350
everything was gonna be okay.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.450
- But that's what's so
beautiful about Swing in general

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.470
is you have to move.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.450
You feel the music as well,
even if you're singing it

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.670
or playing it, it moves you.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.400
And I think that joy and
music sometimes gets lost.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.720
- That's exactly the word, joy.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:07.620
And there's not so much.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.970
A lot of music doesn't have joy in it.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.350
And this music really does, doesn't it?

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:13.110
It's the most and it's been
a very happy experience.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.917
Normally, you hear about
records, people say,

00:08:14.917 --> 00:08:17.850
"Oh, you know, we had
a fight in the studio.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.260
I've left music because of it.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:20.760
It was the worst experience of my life."

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:21.660
This is the opposite.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:22.493
It's been a pleasure.

00:08:22.493 --> 00:08:25.140
It's been so easy 'cause all
the songs, we love the songs

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.760
and it is an expression of joy.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:27.593
So, great.

00:08:27.593 --> 00:08:30.870
- Is it true that y'all did
most of it live in the studio?

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:31.782
Like with the band?
- Yeah.

00:08:31.782 --> 00:08:33.450
- I love that, I've only
done that like a few times

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.590
and God, it is amazing.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:36.870
- Yeah.
- To be in a studio

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:37.703
and feel that.

00:08:37.703 --> 00:08:38.536
- That's the way bands,

00:08:38.536 --> 00:08:40.260
that's the way music used to be recorded.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:42.373
You know, even in the '50s and '60s.

00:08:42.373 --> 00:08:43.320
- Yeah.
- It was all done live.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.560
But the only thing that
wasn't live was my vocal.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.390
I had to have a few goes on
it, get used to the song.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:49.830
Otherwise, it was all live.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:51.720
- That's incredible.
- And it sounds it too.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.100
- There is such a different sound

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.260
and you've been doing
swing for quite some time.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.093
- Yes.

00:08:56.093 --> 00:08:58.736
I mean, I was in this
band, Squeeze, and I left

00:08:58.736 --> 00:09:00.210
and I started a big band in England.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:02.190
- Yeah.
- And I realized, you know,

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:04.200
I had the ability to make
people dance early on,

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.084
I think, you know.

00:09:05.084 --> 00:09:05.917
- Yeah.
- I mean,

00:09:05.917 --> 00:09:07.230
all great musicians or great singers.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:10.080
If Rod connects any song,
that's a great thing.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.270
And I think if you are
me and a piano player,

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.820
you've gotta be able to
make people dance as well.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:15.653
We did.

00:09:16.504 --> 00:09:19.230
As an example, early on in the '90s

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:20.850
when my big band first got together,

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:23.010
we had a show where we did for the G8,

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:25.230
which is all the leaders
of the Western world.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.063
- Yeah.
- So at that time,

00:09:26.063 --> 00:09:27.330
it was President Clinton,

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.790
Prime Minister Blair
and all of the others.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:30.623
- Oh, wow.

00:09:30.623 --> 00:09:32.630
- And we got to do it and we decided--

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.463
- No pressure.

00:09:33.463 --> 00:09:34.296
- No pressure, that's right.

00:09:34.296 --> 00:09:36.677
Exactly, the world's watching
and a lot of security.

00:09:36.677 --> 00:09:37.510
- Yeah.
- But

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.230
we thought we better end with
a song that unifies everybody.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.120
So we did, "All You Need is Love."

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.370
So we play, the trumpet player plays.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:45.203
- Yeah.

00:09:45.203 --> 00:09:47.077
(Jools humming)

00:09:47.077 --> 00:09:48.180
- At which point,

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.250
the French president thinks

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.540
that's a French national anthem.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:52.800
So he stands up.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.120
So then, I'm thinking.
- No.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.230
- Oh, this.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:58.470
And then Blair and Clinton,
both out of politeness,

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:00.150
they stand up 'cause it's
a French national anthem,

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:01.140
sort of doing this.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:03.420
Then it goes into, "All You Need is Love."

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.100
But to avoid an incident,

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.660
and I don't know which one started it

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.393
and credit to him,
whichever one started it.

00:10:08.393 --> 00:10:10.320
They all start doing this.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:11.610
A bit of dad dancing, really.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.443
It was dad dancing.

00:10:12.443 --> 00:10:13.290
- Oh, my God.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.220
I thought you were gonna be like,

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.586
so we broke out with the
French anthem and I was like,

00:10:17.586 --> 00:10:18.932
"You just knew it?"

00:10:18.932 --> 00:10:19.765
- It didn't bother.

00:10:19.765 --> 00:10:20.972
No, no, but it was great.

00:10:20.972 --> 00:10:22.260
And after all, all the world's dancing,

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.527
if they're all dancing, webs
are laughing, aren't we?

00:10:23.527 --> 00:10:24.990
You know.
- Oh, my God.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:25.980
That's hilarious.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.600
What a great story.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.067
And I would be sweating
if I were you to be like,

00:10:30.067 --> 00:10:31.660
"Who knows the anthem?"

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:32.493
(audience laughing)

00:10:32.493 --> 00:10:35.886
♪ What a day this has been ♪

00:10:35.886 --> 00:10:39.239
♪ What a rare mood I'm in ♪

00:10:39.239 --> 00:10:44.239
♪ Why it's all almost like being in love ♪

00:10:45.576 --> 00:10:49.297
♪ There's a smile on my face ♪

00:10:49.297 --> 00:10:52.689
♪ For all human race ♪

00:10:52.689 --> 00:10:57.689
♪ Why it's almost almost
like being in love ♪

00:10:57.814 --> 00:10:59.160
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.532
