in, and started playing.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.043
- I love it.

00:11:22.043 --> 00:11:22.876
- Wonderful.
- It was great.

00:11:22.876 --> 00:11:23.709
- Back to your busking.

00:11:23.709 --> 00:11:24.542
- Yeah.
- I like it.

00:11:24.542 --> 00:11:25.440
- More or less, yes.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:26.670
Kelly, quite right there.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:27.540
- That's amazing though.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.190
Do you see how much joy you
were talking about that earlier.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:30.090
- Yeah.
- And everybody's

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:30.960
just feeling it.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.310
- But also, that song, you see that,

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:35.113
of all the songs on this
record we talked about,

00:11:35.113 --> 00:11:37.980
well, I think of some, so we
just loved all of the songs.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:39.510
This is the one song that I didn't know.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:40.740
I mean, you can't know
everything, can you?

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.210
It's a (indistinct) so I didn't know.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.910
But when, as soon as he starts singing it,

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:46.020
it became my favorite song.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:46.864
You are a great singer.

00:11:46.864 --> 00:11:47.697
You know this.
- Oh, I know that song.

00:11:47.697 --> 00:11:48.960
Yeah.
- But when the singer

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.140
makes you realize, it is
the singer, not the song.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.167
And he's the great singer.

00:11:52.167 --> 00:11:54.600
And this was a particular special moment

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:55.440
when he first sang that.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.405
- Yeah.

00:11:56.405 --> 00:11:59.431
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:11:59.431 --> 00:12:01.018
So you're saying that for the most part,

00:12:01.018 --> 00:12:03.060
y'all agreed on songs or
did you each kind of bring

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.950
your own favorites to the table?

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.030
- Favorites to the table.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:06.863
Yeah.

00:12:06.863 --> 00:12:07.696
- Yeah.
- We didn't know.

00:12:07.696 --> 00:12:08.529
There were no arguments.
- No.

00:12:08.529 --> 00:12:09.362
- Oh, I love that.

00:12:09.362 --> 00:12:11.220
We could have made another
album straight away.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:12.256
- There's so much great music.

00:12:12.256 --> 00:12:13.089
- Yeah, it is.

00:12:13.089 --> 00:12:14.460
- And we both spent a long time living,

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.990
listening to and loving a lot of,

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.670
these are the great old American songs.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.503
- Yeah.
- A couple of 'em

00:12:18.503 --> 00:12:19.494
old English songs, but
most of 'em are great

00:12:19.494 --> 00:12:20.327
old American songs.

00:12:20.327 --> 00:12:21.160
And we've grown up with
all of that, hadn't we?

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.590
- Yeah.
- And just loved them.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:23.797
